      "explanation": "Bevel gears transmit motion between shafts whose axes intersect (usually at right angles), and none of the listed options states this. Parallel axes suit spur or helical gears, non-intersecting axes suit worm or crossed-helical gears, and non-coplanar axes suit hypoid or skew gears, so the printed options (page 8 of the 2010 Mechanical Engineering Paper-II) do not include the correct relationship.",
